First, let's solve the system of equations. We have:
\begin{align*}
4u-5v&=23 \\
2u+4v&=-8
\end{align*}

To eliminate one of the variables, we can multiply the second equation by $2$:
\begin{align*}
4u-5v&=23 \\
4u+8v&=-16
\end{align*}

Now, subtract the first equation from the second equation:
\begin{align*}
(4u+8v)-(4u-5v) &= -16-23 \\
13v &= -39 \\
v &= -3
\end{align*}

Substitute $v=-3$ back into one of the original equations to find $u$. Let's use the second equation:
\begin{align*}
2u+4(-3) &= -8 \\
2u-12 &= -8 \\
2u &= 4 \\
u &= 2
\end{align*}

Now that we have $u=2$ and $v=-3$, we can find $u+v$:
\begin{align*}
u+v &= 2+(-3) \\
&= -1
\end{align*}

Therefore, the value of $u+v$ is $\boxed{-1}$.
